text:
Styling and layout
The site uses Quarto’s default theme in light mode and a dark version of it in dark mode. theme: picks others from Quarto’s built-in themes, with quartodown’s styling on top:
theme:
  light: flatly
  dark: darkly
A theme can also be your own .scss file in _quartodown/, such as light: _quartodown/brand.scss. To adjust a built-in theme, use extra.scss (see below).






TipA crowded navbar





Some themes space the navbar’s items further apart or capitalize them. With lux, for example, “Get started” wraps onto two lines and the version is cut off. Bringing the items closer in _quartodown/extra.scss fixes it:
/*-- scss:rules --*/
.navbar .nav-item {
  margin-right: 0.25rem;
}

.navbar .nav-link,
.navbar-brand {
  white-space: nowrap;
}



To restyle every page, add _quartodown/extra.scss. It applies to both the light and the dark theme, and has two sections:

scss:defaults sets variables, such as colors and fonts, that the theme uses throughout.
scss:rules holds CSS rules, which can use those variables.

/*-- scss:defaults --*/
1$primary: #2c7a7b;
$font-family-sans-serif: "Inter", sans-serif;

/*-- scss:rules --*/
.navbar {
2  border-bottom: 1px solid $border-color;
}

1

Links, the active navbar item and buttons.

2

$border-color is the light theme’s in light mode and the dark theme’s in dark mode.


Plain CSS can go in _quartodown/extra.css instead, which is added to every page as it is.
The page’s widths and spacing are Quarto settings, under quarto:. For example, a wider text column and table of contents:
quarto:
  format:
    html:
      grid:
        body-width: 900px
        margin-width: 300px
See Quarto’s page layout guide for grid: and page-layout:.

The logo
The package’s logo, man/figures/logo.svg (or logo.png), shows right of every page’s title, except on pages that show it already, such as a home page whose README has it in its title. If there is also a man/figures/logo-light.svg (or .png), light mode shows that one instead. The site’s favicon is logo.png (or logo.svg). To leave the logo off the pages:
logo: false
The navbar’s items start where the page’s text does, which a script on each page measures. To start them at the edge of the page instead, override it with:
/*-- scss:rules --*/
.navbar-container {
  padding-left: 1em !important;
}
Everything in _quartodown/ is copied into the Quarto project, so other files it holds can be named from quarto: by the same path, such as Quarto template partials:
quarto:
  format:
    html:
      template-partials:
        - _quartodown/title-block.html
Setting include-in-header: or include-after-body: replaces quartodown’s own files, which, among other things, pick dark mode for visitors who prefer it and line up the navbar. To add to them, list them too:
quarto:
  format:
    html:
      include-in-header:
        - quartodown-header.html
        - _quartodown/analytics.html

Every page, help pages included, is a Quarto page, so you get:

every Quarto feature, from callouts and tabsets to code annotations and cross-references, on every page;
Quarto’s themes, extensions and settings.

On top of that, quartodown adds:

the package website layout R users know from pkgdown: a home page sidebar, a grouped function reference, articles and a changelog;
function links with hover tooltips.

A custom look
Your own .scss files as themes set the colors, here a blue tint in light mode and a navy page in dark mode. _quartodown/extra.scss restyles any part of the site in both: here rounder code blocks and the function reference as cards.








NoteThe settings





_quartodown/_quartodown.yml:
theme:
  light: _quartodown/blue-light.scss
  dark: _quartodown/blue-dark.scss
_quartodown/blue-dark.scss:
/*-- scss:defaults --*/
// The same blue on a navy page.
$primary: #7fb3e6;
$link-color: $primary;
$body-bg: #10161d;
$body-color: #d6dde5;
$headings-color: #f0f4f8;
$text-muted: #9aa8b6;
$border-color: #6b7a8a;
$code-color: #c3b1e8;
$code-bg: $body-bg;
$code-block-bg: #18212b;
$pre-color: inherit;

// Bootstrap's defaults for these are meant for a light page.
$input-bg: #1c2530;
$popover-bg: #1c2530;
$footer-bg: $body-bg;
$dropdown-bg: $body-bg;
$dropdown-color: $body-color;
$dropdown-link-color: $body-color;
$dropdown-link-hover-color: $headings-color;
$dropdown-link-hover-bg: #2a3542;
$nav-tabs-link-active-color: $body-color;
_quartodown/blue-light.scss:
/*-- scss:defaults --*/
// A cool, blue-tinted page.
$primary: #1f5f99;
$link-color: $primary;
$body-bg: #f6f8fb;
$body-color: #1c2733;
$headings-color: #12283f;
$border-color: #c5d0dc;
$code-color: #7a3e9d;
$code-block-bg: #e8eef5;
_quartodown/extra.scss:
/*-- scss:rules --*/
// Rounder code blocks, marked with the accent.
div.sourceCode {
  border-radius: 0.75rem;
  border-left: 4px solid $primary;
}

// Each function on the reference index as a card, below the logo.
dl.ref-index {
  clear: both;
}

dl.ref-index dt,
dl.ref-index dd {
  background: rgba($body-color, 0.04);
  border: 1px solid rgba($body-color, 0.1);
  padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
}

dl.ref-index dt {
  border-bottom: none;
  border-radius: 0.75rem 0.75rem 0 0;
}

dl.ref-index dd {
  border-top: none;
  border-radius: 0 0 0.75rem 0.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}
